<back><div type="verses">
<lg label="2."><l>To Thee I owe my wealth, and friends,</l><l>And health, and safe abode;</l><l>Thanks to Thy name for meaner things,</l><l>But they are not my God.</l><l>How vain a toy is glittering wealth,</l><l>If once compared to Thee!</l><l>Or what’s my safety, or my health,</l><l>Or all my friends to me.</l></lg>
<lg label="3."><l>Were I possessor of the earth,</l><l>And called the stars my own,</l><l>Without Thy graces and Thyself,</l><l>I were a wretch undone.</l><l>Let others stretch their arms like seas,</l><l>And grasp in all the shore;</l><l>Grant me the visits of Thy grace,</l><l>And I desire no more.</l></lg>
</div>
</back>
</music></mei>
